  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe displayed mill envelope starts on the Z=0 table plane.\nIt keeps its full Z travel height.\nX/Y keep the setup work origin as their reference.\nLathe cylinders keep their existing reference.\nThe tooltip states these references.\nThe decision record is in `docs/decisions/1963-envelope-table.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe viewport drew the program-space travel bounds directly.\nThose bounds can extend below the table plane.\nWith `assets/machines/tormach-pcnc1100-s3.mch`, the fresh document implicit setup drew its bottom at Z=-419.1 mm.\nX/Y have no equivalent height error against the table plane.\nThe current machine files do not state a table footprint for another X/Y reference.\n\nNo travel or reach check uses the drawn box.\n`crates/post/src/machine/envelope.rs` supplies display data only.\nThe travel check in `crates/app/src/machine/mod.rs` reads axis limits and program coordinates directly.\nThis fix changes no safety check.\n\n## Viewport screenshots\n\nBoth images use the Tormach PCNC 1100 Series 3 machine file.\nBoth use a fresh document, the implicit setup, and the world origin.\nThe work envelope is visible in both images.\nThe GPU viewport and the application UI render at 1440 × 960 pixels.\nThe camera stays fixed: target [0, 0, 180] mm, yaw 0.9 rad, pitch 0.5 rad, distance 2400 mm.\nA temporary test fixture captured the application UI and GPU viewport.\nThe fixture was removed after capture.\n\nBefore: the display shift is reverted. The box bottom is Z=-419.1 mm.\n\n![Before: envelope below the table plane](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/2006/before.png)\n\nAfter: the reviewed fix is restored. The box bottom is Z=0 mm.\n\n![After: envelope starts at the table plane](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/2006/after.png)\n\nThe images are stored only on the fork's `pr-screenshots` branch.\nThe PR branch contains no screenshot files.\n\n## Tests\n\n`mill_envelope_stands_on_table_for_all_travel_files` failed before the fix.\nIt checks each bundled box envelope with complete travel limits.\nIt pins the bottom at Z=0, the travel height, and the existing X/Y bounds.\n\n`mill_envelope_stays_on_table_with_shifted_origin_and_inverted_z` failed before the fix.\nIt checks G54 at [10, 20, 70] mm with standard and inverted Z.\n\nFor mutation testing, I restored the original module from `upstream/main`.\nBoth pins failed again.\nI restored the fix, and both pins passed.\nAll five envelope tests passed.\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed.\nIt ran 817 unit tests and 25 integration tests.\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\n`git diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\"` is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nI did not run the native application or the pixel snapshot lane.\nI did not run the release gate or physical machine motion.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone found in the file overlap checks.\n\nChangelog: Place the displayed mill work envelope on the table plane and preserve its travel height.\n\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #1963\n\n",
